# Reuse and Composition Limits — `actions`

Apply this rule for every code-change task.

## Reuse first

- Before creating new logic/UI, check if an existing function, hook, utility, or component can be reused or extended.
- Prefer shared, parameterized building blocks instead of duplicated near-identical implementations.

## Parameter and complexity limits

- Functions should preferably have up to 3 arguments.
- Absolute function limit is 5 arguments. Beyond that, redesign by splitting responsibilities and/or introducing a typed options object.
- If a component requires around 15 independent props/controls, split it into two or more focused components.

## Practical guidance

- Do not create a "god" component/function controlled by many toggles.
- When in doubt, choose composability: smaller pieces with clear contracts.
